{
  "description": "The CXC v0.2.40 -> CRW rename table as data (Wave 0 name-substitution.md and cli-names.md, with the decisions of decisions.md). A Go replayer applies `rules` in order to a fixture's expected text, tree paths and tree contents (never to the fixture file), after normalisation.json. Regex rules use Go regexp (RE2) syntax and Go replacement templates (${1} is a group, $$ a literal dollar); a rule with repeat is applied until the text stops changing, because RE2 has no lookaround and a captured boundary character cannot start the next match. resolver and rewrite rules are not plain text edits: their note says what replaces the text. `cli` maps the argv prefix of each cxc step to the crw command; the rest of argv is kept. `never` lists text no rule may touch, `input_side` the recognizers whose rename changes what is accepted, `env` and `skills` the renamed names. Hook legs keep their declarations (decision 3: 32 registrations, statusMessage R24, the command becomes the crw hook entry for that leg).",
